-- ============================================================================
-- carbon EXPERT DEEP SEED: Carbon & Energy Efficiency, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE CURVE AND THE PATH. The cost of a tonne abated,
-- capital annualised over the measure's life by a capital recovery factor; a
-- negative cost that pays for itself; the marginal abatement cost curve ranked
-- cheapest first with its weighted average; measures that interact and claims
-- above what a source emits; a target on a partial inventory; the path and its
-- unabated gap; one saving priced in money and carbon from the same energy;
-- energy intensity against a peer the plant has the right to use.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A blank capital cost is not free, a blank
-- rate is not 0, a rate is a fraction, and a curve whose claims exceed what a
-- source emits gives no verdict.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A one-off capital cost set against one year's
-- saving overstates the cost per tonne of a capital measure.
--
-- No NPV, IRR, Monte Carlo or decision tree is taught or graded; the levelised
-- cost per tonne is. The capstone grades four costs in US dollars per tonne and
-- one net annual cost in US dollars at 0.01, and one unabated gap in tCO2e at
-- 0.01.
-- ============================================================================

values ('carbon', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-cost-of-a-tonne-abated","title":"The Cost of a Tonne Abated","lesson_keys":["l01-capital-recovery","l02-a-negative-cost-pays-for-itself","l03-a-blank-is-not-free","l04-a-rate-is-a-fraction","l05-one-year-against-a-life"]},{"key":"m02-the-marginal-abatement-cost-curve","title":"The Marginal Abatement Cost Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-cheapest-first","l02-steps-that-tile-the-axis","l03-the-weighted-average","l04-measures-that-pay-for-themselves"]},{"key":"m03-interactions-and-over-claims","title":"Interactions and Over-claims","lesson_keys":["l01-two-measures-on-one-source","l02-claims-above-what-a-source-emits","l03-a-verdict-left-unassessed","l04-a-source-with-no-emission-passed"]},{"key":"m04-targets-and-the-path","title":"Targets and the Path","lesson_keys":["l01-a-target-on-a-partial-inventory","l02-a-straight-line-to-the-end-year","l03-the-unabated-gap","l04-measures-with-no-start-year","l05-the-first-shortfall-year"]},{"key":"m05-savings-into-the-ledger","title":"Savings into the Ledger","lesson_keys":["l01-one-saving-in-money-and-carbon","l02-the-heating-value-basis","l03-the-cost-per-tonne-handed-over","l04-the-simple-payback","l05-energy-intensity-and-its-peer"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-agbor-programme-end-to-end","l02-what-is-held-and-what-is-decided","l03-what-the-oracles-check"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
